  "compare_constants_O2_range_folded": {
    "note": "Hand-derived from the C source plus the unsigned range identity lo <= x <= hi  <=>  (unsigned)(x - lo) <= (hi - lo). GCC -O2 folds two-sided range checks (and length == 0 || length >= 32) into one subtraction and one unsigned comparison, so the literal source constants of compare_constants do not exist in the -O2 binary. A check passes when, in that function, a stated branch/conditional-move relation compares a register with span (<=) or span+1 (<) as unsigned, and that register (or a sub-register of the same family) was produced by an instruction subtracting lo (LEA displacement -lo or SUB lo). objdump_confirmation addresses were read from GNU objdump output of aire_test_binary_O2 and are documentation, not used for scoring.",
